{
    "background_story": "Heaven was a secluded beach town on the coast, known for its crystal-clear waters and pristine shores. The town's unique geography made it an ideal location for the production of iodine, a valuable resource extracted from the seaweed that grew abundantly in the area. The iodine industry brought prosperity to the town, earning it the nickname 'Iodinated Heaven'. As the years passed, the town became a hub for scientific research, attracting experts in the field of iodine production and its applications. The town's iodinated waters were said to have healing properties, drawing visitors from all over the world seeking relief from various ailments. Despite the influx of tourists, Heaven remained a tranquil haven, its iodinated waters a reminder of the town's rich history and natural bounty.",
